        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Glenn Quagmire, Seth MacFarlane\n- Works: Family Guy, Ted, Ted 2, A Million Ways to Die in the West\n- Concepts: Character description, 1950s party-animal clichés\n\nFacts:\n- Seth MacFarlane wrote, directed, and starred in the film \"Ted\" in 2012.\n- Seth MacFarlane wrote, directed, and starred in the film \"A Million Ways to Die in the West\" in 2014.\n- Seth MacFarlane wrote, directed, and starred in the film \"Ted 2\" in 2015.\n- Seth MacFarlane is the creator and voice actor of Glenn Quagmire on Family Guy.\n- Seth MacFarlane described Glenn Quagmire as \"an appalling human being who is still caught in the rat-pack era.\"\n- Seth MacFarlane said Glenn Quagmire is based on anachronistic 1950s party-animal clichés.",
